---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.config';

const { googleAnalyticsId, microsoftClarityId, cloudflareAnalyticsToken } = SITE.analytics;
const analyticsEnabled = Boolean(
  googleAnalyticsId || microsoftClarityId || cloudflareAnalyticsToken
);
---

<PageLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description={`Which cookies and local storage ${SITE.name} uses, what each one does, which are optional, and how to control them in your browser.`}
  lede="What we store on your device, and why."
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-08-02')}
>
  <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-warning)]/40 bg-[var(--color-warning)]/10 p-4 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">
    <strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Note:</strong> this page describes what this
    deployment actually sets. If you operate the site and enable an analytics provider,
    update the tables below to match.
  </div>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} sets <strong>no advertising cookies and no cross-site tracking cookies</strong>.
    The site is statically hosted and has no reader accounts, so there is no session cookie
    either. The only thing stored by default is your light/dark theme preference, and it
    never leaves your browser.
  </p>
  <p>
    {
      analyticsEnabled
        ? 'An analytics provider is currently enabled on this deployment, so measurement storage described below may also be present.'
        : 'No analytics provider is currently configured, so none of the optional analytics storage described below is being set at all.'
    }
  </p>

  <h2>Cookie categories</h2>
  <p>
    Everything this site could store falls into one of four categories. Two of them are
    permanently empty.
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full border-collapse text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-[var(--bg-alt)]">
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Category</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Used here?</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">What it covers</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Consent</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><strong>Strictly necessary</strong></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Yes</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Bot mitigation and rate limiting set by our CDN so pages can be served safely
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Not required</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><strong>Preferences</strong></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Yes</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Your theme choice, stored locally so the site does not flash the wrong mode on
            the next visit
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Set only when you choose a theme</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><strong>Analytics</strong></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            {analyticsEnabled ? 'Yes — see below' : 'Not currently'}
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Aggregate page views and interaction data, only if a provider ID is configured
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Optional</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><strong>Advertising / tracking</strong></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">No</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Ad targeting, retargeting pixels, cross-site profiling — none of this is used
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Never set</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What is stored, item by item</h2>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full border-collapse text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-[var(--bg-alt)]">
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Name</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Type</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Purpose</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Duration</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><code>theme</code></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Local storage (first party)</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Remembers whether you chose light or dark mode. Never sent to a server.
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Until you clear it</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><code>__cf_bm</code> / <code>_cfuvid</code></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Cookie (Cloudflare)</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Bot management and rate limiting by our hosting provider
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Session / 30 minutes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><code>_ga</code> / <code>_ga_*</code></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Cookie (Google Analytics 4)</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Distinguishes visits for aggregate reporting. Only set if a GA4 measurement ID
            is configured — {googleAnalyticsId ? 'currently enabled.' : 'currently disabled.'}
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Up to 2 years</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><code>_clck</code> / <code>_clsk</code></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Cookie (Microsoft Clarity)</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Aggregate interaction and scroll measurement used to find broken pages. Only set
            if a Clarity project ID is configured —
            {microsoftClarityId ? ' currently enabled.' : ' currently disabled.'}
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Up to 1 year / 1 day</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">None</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Cloudflare Web Analytics</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Cookieless page-view counting. Sets no cookie and no local storage. Only loaded
            if a beacon token is configured —
            {cloudflareAnalyticsToken ? ' currently enabled.' : ' currently disabled.'}
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Not applicable</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Optional analytics, in plain terms</h2>
  <p>
    Analytics on this site is optional infrastructure. When no provider ID is set in the
    site configuration, no analytics script is injected into the page and your browser
    never contacts the provider. When one is set, it is used only to see which articles are
    read and which pages are broken — never for advertising, never shared with ad networks,
    and never used to identify you personally. Whatever is active is named in the
    <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party requests</h2>
  <p>
    Web fonts are requested from Google Fonts. This sets no cookie, but the request
    necessarily discloses your IP address to that service as a technical consequence of
    delivering the font file. Embedded content, where an article includes it, may set
    cookies under the embedding provider's own policy.
  </p>

  <h2>How to control this</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Block or delete cookies</strong> — every major browser supports this under
      Privacy or Site Settings, per site or globally.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Clear local storage</strong> — this resets your theme preference, after which
      the site follows your operating system setting again.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Opt out of GA4 specifically</strong> — Google publishes a browser add-on that
      blocks its analytics scripts everywhere, if that provider is ever enabled here.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Use a content blocker</strong> — a standard tracker blocker removes the
      optional analytics requests entirely.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site breaks if you block all storage. Articles, the
    <a href="/tools/">tool directory</a>, <a href="/search/">search</a> and the
    <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> all work without it. The only visible difference is
    that your theme choice will not persist between visits.
  </p>

  <h2>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h2>
  <p>
    We do not perform cross-site tracking, so a DNT or GPC signal changes nothing about how
    we treat you. There is no profile to opt out of.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about anything on this page:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.organization.email}`}>{SITE.organization.email}</a>, or use the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
